{"name":"Pitcher","hex":"#b5d1be","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Pitcher","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname.","A place in the United States:\nA township in Cherokee County, Iowa.\nA town and hamlet therein, in Chenango County, New York, named after Nathaniel Pitcher."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Pitcher"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pitcher","blocks":[{"text":"In baseball, the pitcher is the player who throws (\"pitches\") the baseball from the pitcher's mound toward the catcher to begin each play, with the goal of retiring a batter, who attempts to either make contact with the pitched ball or draw a walk. In the defensive numbering system used in baseball, the pitcher is assigned the number 1. The pitcher is often considered the most important player on the defensive side of the game, and as such is situated at the right end of the defensive spectrum. There are many different types of pitchers, such as the starting pitcher, relief pitcher, middle reliever, lefty specialist, setup man, and the closer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/70/Clayton_Kershaw_on_July_23%2C_2015_%282%29.jpg/330px-Clayton_Kershaw_on_July_23%2C_2015_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pitcher","wikidata":"Q1048902"},{"title":"Pitcher (container)","blocks":[{"text":"In American English, a pitcher is a container with a handle and a spout, used for storing and pouring liquids. In English-speaking countries outside North America, such a container is called a jug."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Ewer_and_basin_MET_DP362783_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Ewer_and_basin_MET_DP362783_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pitcher_(container)","wikidata":"Q132397"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikime